</figure>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Explanation:</span>
Here, <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> is the problem dimension or latent space dimension; <math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of time steps for the token dynamics (<a href="#S1.E3" title="In 1 Introduction ‣ Sparse Transformer Architectures via Regularized Wasserstein Proximal Operator with 𝐿_1 Prior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>); <math id="A2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> is the coefficients for the HJB regularizer in (<a href="#S2.E16" title="In 2.4 Learning objective and training procedure ‣ 2 Proposed network structure and PDE formulation ‣ Sparse Transformer Architectures via Regularized Wasserstein Proximal Operator with 𝐿_1 Prior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>); width is the number of neurons per layer; <math id="A2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\mathrm{iters}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>iters</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\mathrm{iters}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the total number of training iterations; batch size is the number of samples per iteration; the learning rate shows the initial and final values; noise indicates the noise level in the training data. Moreover, we set <math id="A2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=1</annotation></semantics></math> for the initialization.</p>
</div>
</section>
